      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:z06xie'
    '|a||Governments do it on a grand scale. Britain and France kept paying for Concorde long after it was clear it would never pay its way, and biologists named the error after it: the Concorde fallacy.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1fydpg3'
    '|b||But don''t call every stubborn firm a fool. Avinash Dixit showed that when prices jump about and restarting is costly, a firm can be right to stay open even when the price dips a little below AVC.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1cttkaq'
    '|a||Because closing has costs of its own: a crew that leaves, customers who go elsewhere, a costly restart. Waiting can be worth it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:j30d64'
    '|b||How sure are we? That sunk costs should not steer a choice: consensus. That producers behave that way: mostly agreed. In Texas, oil from existing wells barely responds to price; drilling does.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 14520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1a1nk5z'
    '|a||That people fall for the fallacy: contested. In careful lab games the effect turned out small and patchy.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1s5zq6v'
    '|a||Three new cases. A ski resort has a warm winter. Lift tickets bring in $8,000 a day; staff and power for the lifts cost $6,000 a day; the loan on the lifts costs $5,000 a day, open or shut. Open for the season?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 15160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1mdakxi'
    '|a||Yes: open it loses $3,000 a day, shut it loses the whole $5,000 loan payment.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Open it loses $3,000 a day, shut it loses the whole $5,000 loan payment.':
